			"notes": "## Balancing update\n\n**Full release!**\n\n~: Reworked time dilation. Instead of straight up blocking item usage and cooldowns, now makes it take twice as long.\n~: Changed pharaohvisual command to only allow players with cheats to access.\n~: Increased the duration between ranged attacks of the pharaoh (2s -> 3.5s)\n-: Removed enchantments from the bow of the Unburied (was just a little too overpowered)\n-: Removed tipped arrows from the ranged Unburied (they default to weakness)\n+: Added more sand piles per desert temple, and a higher amount of guaranteed hieroglyph tablets per temple\n~: Reworked sacred gold upgrade smithing template to no longer require hieroglyph tablets\n~: Reworked sacred gold upgrade smithing template to accept desert-related trim templates instead of the netherite upgrade one\n+: Added reroll_pharaoh_summon command, which rerolls the summoning requirements for the world\n~: Changed some of the translations for hints (they were too vague)\n~: Reworked sacred gold upgrade smithing template recipe advancement to trigger when obtaining alternative templates, as well as when obtaining sacred gemstone\n+: Added alternative items to the list of summoning requirements, more specifically wither skeleton skulls instead of skeleton skulls, enchanted golden apples instead of golden apples, ominous trial keys instead of trial keys, eye armor trim smithing templates instead of hieroglyph tablets"
		},
